= Implementation <ch:implementation>

This chapter describes the software that implements the methods of @ch:numerics. The code is a Python package, `nbody`, built on NumPy @harris2020array, with Matplotlib @hunter2007matplotlib for plots and pygame for the interactive viewer. SciPy @virtanen2020scipy is used only to compute independent reference solutions. The design follows four goals:

+ *Correctness.* Every theoretical property claimed in @ch:numerics (order, symplecticity, reversibility, cost) is checked by an automated test.
+ *Extensibility.* New integrators, force laws and scenarios can be added without modifying existing code.
+ *Efficiency.* All numerical kernels operate on whole arrays; no Python loop runs over bodies or pairs.
+ *Reproducibility.* Every figure and table in @ch:evaluation is regenerated by a single command and read directly by this document.

