The experiments of @ch:evaluation are Python modules (`experiments/e01_*.py` to `e09_*.py`). `python -m experiments.run_all` runs all of them in about six minutes on a laptop. They write SVG figures to `thesis/figures/generated` and CSV/JSON tables to `thesis/data`, which this document reads with Typst's `csv()` and `json()` functions. Random initial conditions use fixed seeds. The numerical results are therefore deterministic; only wall-clock timings depend on the machine.

